.\" The date is this page's own last non-trivial change, per man-pages(7),
.\" not the build date.
.TH FRAMEGUIN 1 2026-08-26 "Frameguin @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
frameguin \- hardware controls for Framework laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frameguin
.RI [ OPTION .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B frameguin
manages the hardware settings of a Framework laptop, from a window or a
tray icon.
.PP
The application itself is unprivileged. Hardware access happens in
.BR frameguin\-daemon ,
a root daemon on the system bus that systemd starts on demand, and every
state\-changing call is authorized through polkit. Controls appear only for
the operations the board answers to, so an unsupported machine shows fewer
of them rather than failing.
.PP
Run without options,
.B frameguin
opens its window. Closing the window hides it to the tray where one exists;
.B Quit
in the tray or the main menu exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-info
Print the board, both binaries' versions and the paths they ran from, the EC
firmware version, and the capabilities the daemon probed successfully. This
is what to include in a bug report; the same text is behind the copy button
on the About window's Troubleshooting page.
.IP
Two different path prefixes in the output mean two installations are present
and shadowing each other.
.TP
.B \-\-gapplication\-service
Start in service mode, registering the tray icon without opening a window.
The autostart entry uses this; it is not normally typed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.valeronm.Frameguin.desktop
Written and removed by the
.B Start at login
switch.
.TP
.I /var/lib/frameguin/state
Haptic touchpad settings the daemon remembers, because the firmware will not
report them back.
.SH NOTES
A battery charge limit set here lasts until reboot. UEFI setup re-sends its
own stored value at every power-on, so the standing limit lives in BIOS
setup rather than here.
.PP
A touchscreen switched off comes back on when the lid is opened, after a
suspend, and at the next restart. The panel's enable is a line the firmware
re-asserts rather than a setting anything stores, so nothing carries the
choice across.
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/valeronm/frameguin/issues
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The daemon logs through the journal:
.B journalctl -u frameguin-daemon.service
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR polkit (8)
